      "side": 1,
      "message": "What\u0027s the advantage of creating a new driver to allocate cma memory instead of using dmabuf cma heap?",
      "revId": "31dcae769791c14068db45925c7973258daf8ba1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0fe2fff5_2c863d5b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1889140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-06T02:37:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The main advantage is that the driver allows to debug early on CMA allocations before init starts.\n\nIn the userspace, we can use dma cma heaps instead.\n\n\nNote: I don\u0027t intend to upstream the driver. It will only live in the `main-16k-gs-shusky-5.15` repo, which it is only for experiments.",
      "parentUuid": "866e9ec2_b00786ff",
      "revId": "31dcae769791c14068db45925c7973258daf8ba1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8b7e011a_1ca4c854",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1157738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-06T18:21:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "re: the driver allows to debug early on CMA allocations before init starts\n\nWhy is it important to test these allocations before init starts? IIUC the only difference is that CMA will not be polluted at that time but is that important?",
      "parentUuid": "0fe2fff5_2c863d5b",
      "revId": "31dcae769791c14068db45925c7973258daf8ba1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0c286ceb_2cdde528",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1889140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-07T01:37:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Why is it important to test these allocations before init starts?\n\nThe main difference is that:\n\n- in userspace, the allocations comes from this CMA heap `dma_contiguous_default_area`:\nhttps://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/v6.13.5/source/kernel/dma/contiguous.c#L55\nand the default size is 4MiB in 4Kib kernels and 32MiB in 16KiB kernels. This can be overwritten by the cma\u003dsize kernel parameter.\nhttps://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/v6.13.5/source/kernel/dma/contiguous.c#L223\n\n- in the driver, the CMA allocations comes from the reserve memory in the device tree:\n\n```\n\t\tcma_test_reserve: cma_test_reserve {\n\t\t\tcompatible \u003d \"shared-dma-pool\";\n\t\t\treusable;\n\t\t\tsize \u003d \u003c0x0 0x2000000\u003e; /* 32 MiB */\n\t\t\talignment \u003d \u003c0x0 0x00001000\u003e;\n\t\t\talloc-ranges \u003d \u003c0x0 0x9 0x80000000 0x80000000\u003e,\n\t\t\t\t       \u003c0x0 0x9 0x00000000 0x80000000\u003e;\n\t\t};\n```\n\nThe dma heap allocations can\u0027t come from the reserve CMA allocations in DTS in vanilla kernels.",
      "parentUuid": "8b7e011a_1ca4c854",
      "revId": "31dcae769791c14068db45925c7973258daf8ba1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "096a20e8_e1beb50e",
